    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d843">

                <pb facs="0900" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg812"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grip to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Sweden and Norway</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March 9,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have had the honor of
                    receiving your kind personal letter of the 5th instant, relating to the generous
                    action taken by the United States Government as to the Norwegian steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Farmand</hi> in Santo Domingan waters, and I venture to
                    express my profound thanks for your courtesy.</p>
                <p>The New York charterers of the <hi rendition="#italic">Farmand</hi>, Hugh Kelly
                    &amp; Co., now inform me that another Norwegian steamer, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hugin</hi>, which is also chartered by them, will also, on or about the
                    20th instant, arrive at the port of Macoris, in order to load a cargo of sugar
                    owned by another firm of New York.</p>
                <p>I take the great liberty to ask whether it would be possible that the good
                    offices of the United States Government might kindly be extended to the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hugin</hi> on her arrival at the port of Macoris.</p>
                <p>I beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Grip.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
